&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the AI Security Institute&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI Security Institute is the world&#39;s largest and best-funded team dedicated to understanding advanced AI risks and translating that knowledge into action. We’re in the heart of the UK government with direct lines to No. 10 (the Prime Minister&#39;s office), and we work with frontier developers and governments globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re here because governments are critical for advanced AI going well, and UK AISI is uniquely positioned to mobilise them. With our resources, unique agility and international influence, this is the best place to shape both AI development and government action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;The deadline for applying to this role is Sunday 29th November 2026, end of day, anywhere on Earth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AISI&#39;s Technical Standards and Best Practice team identifies what best practice is needed to manage the most serious risks from frontier AI development and leverages AISI’s position to get it adopted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI capabilities are advancing faster than the science and practices used to manage their risks. Risks now emerge earlier, during training, internal deployment and evaluation, not just at public release, and evaluation methods are struggling to keep pace. Yet there is no consensus on the set of practices needed to safely use and develop the most capable AI systems, and high-level principles are not enough to manage these risks. What&#39;s needed is concrete technical guidance that developers agree is necessary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AISI is uniquely placed to lead on parts of this industry-wide effort to establish best practice. We house researchers with state-of-the-art technical insight on keeping AI secure during internal use, hold existing relationships with industry and other frontier AI organisations, and offer a neutral third-party home to establish best practice collaboratively. This role directly delivers on part of the&amp;nbsp;Prime Minister’s September 2026&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;commitment that the UK will work towards principles and standards that ensure the most capable AI systems are developed securely and with appropriate transparency. It builds &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;directly on our October 2026 publication &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aisi.gov.uk/blog/towards-technical-best-practice-for-frontier-ai-development&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-con

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About BakerHicks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BakerHicks is a leading design, engineering and project delivery consultancy, delivering complex infrastructure, industrial and built environment projects across the UK and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Infrastructure team supports a wide range of clients and frameworks, providing specialist engineering, inspection, surveying and asset management services. As our project portfolio continues to grow, we are expanding our network of trusted contractors to support current and future bridge inspection requirements across the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength lies in our collaborative approach, technical excellence, and ability to mobilise the right expertise at pace to support our clients’ requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Bridges Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BakerHicks, our Bridges Team delivers expert engineering solutions across the full lifecycle of bridge and structures projects, from inspection and assessment through to design, refurbishment, strengthening, and replacement works. Our engineers work on a diverse portfolio of assets including highway bridges, railway bridges, footbridges, retaining structures, culverts, and other critical infrastructure across the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We combine technical excellence with a practical, collaborative approach, working closely with clients, asset owners, local authorities, contractors, and multidisciplinary teams to develop safe, sustainable, and cost-effective solutions. Our experience spans inspections, structural assessments, repair schemes, asset management programmes, and the delivery of complex infrastructure projects in highly regulated environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking Expressions of Interest from competent and experienced Bridge and Structural Inspectors to join our growing contractor talent pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a live vacancy tied to a specific project. Instead, we are building a network of pre-qualified professionals who can be considered for assignments as needs arise across our infrastructure portfolio.&lt;br&gt;Applications are welcomed from anywhere in the UK. Site travel will normally be required, there is no requirement to be based near a BakerHicks office.&lt;/p&gt;
